git squash : combine multiple commints into one clear commit .

git merge  vs  git rebase  
        merge : combines changes from branch to the target branch ( keep branch commits history)
        rebase : combines changes from branch to the top of target brach ( linear history ) 

git help : opens manual page for git commit

git cherry-pick : copy changes from specific commit to the target branch

git clean : deletes untracked folders and directory

git grep : searched for text accros the tracked files

git blame : who last changed each line of this file 

git bisect : find the commit that causes the bug

git shortlog : who made the commits

git prune : remove unreachable git objects

git worktree : creating multiple folders for the same repo

git verify-commit : verify the author

git filter-repo : permanently deleting file from the whole commits history
